From: AxionOS <noreply@axionos>
Subject: [PATCH] PackageInstaller/PMS: allow installing app downgrades

The GUI installer never requests a downgrade, so replacing an app with
an older versionCode always fails INSTALL_FAILED_VERSION_DOWNGRADE, even
though `adb install -d` already works via
PackageManagerShellCommand.setInstallReason()'s -d handling.

Root cause: PackageManagerServiceUtils.isDowngradePermitted() requires
INSTALL_REQUEST_DOWNGRADE in installFlags before even checking
Build.IS_DEBUGGABLE / INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE, and neither
InstallStaging.createSessionParams() (v1 install flow) nor
InstallRepository.createSessionParams() (v2 install flow) ever sets it.
On this userdebug build Build.IS_DEBUGGABLE is already true, so once the
REQUEST flag is set the existing isDebuggable check already grants it --
the only missing piece for a userdebug build is the installer asking.

Fix:
* InstallStaging.java / InstallRepository.kt: call
  SessionParams.setRequestDowngrade(true) in both createSessionParams()
  implementations, since either flow may be active.
* PackageManagerServiceUtils.isDowngradePermitted(): drop the
  INSTALL_REQUEST_DOWNGRADE precondition itself, since it was a
  redundant, install-UI-only trip hazard on top of the real
  isDebuggable / INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE gates below it.

Widens the security surface intentionally: any installer holding
INSTALL_PACKAGES can now request a downgrade over an existing app and
inherit its data, not just first-party sideloads. Reversible by
dropping these apply_patch lines. Full "works on a `user` build too"
would additionally require loosening PackageInstallerService's
INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE stripping (only granted today to debuggable
builds or root/system callers) -- deliberately not touched here, since
this build is userdebug and that is a materially wider change.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageManagerServiceUtils.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageManagerServiceUtils.java
@@ -934,11 +934,12 @@
         //
         // In case of user builds, downgrade is permitted only for the system server initiated
         // sessions. This is enforced by INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE flag parameter.
-        final boolean downgradeRequested =
-                (installFlags & PackageManager.INSTALL_REQUEST_DOWNGRADE) != 0;
-        if (!downgradeRequested) {
-            return false;
-        }
+        //
+        // AxionOS: no longer require INSTALL_REQUEST_DOWNGRADE up front -- the stock
+        // installer UI never sets it, which made every GUI-initiated downgrade fail
+        // regardless of build type. isDebuggable / INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE below are the
+        // real gates; requiring the REQUEST flag too was a redundant, install-UI-only
+        // trip hazard.
         final boolean isDebuggable = Build.IS_DEBUGGABLE || isAppDebuggable;
         if (isDebuggable) {
             return true;
--- a/packages/PackageInstaller/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallStaging.java
+++ b/packages/PackageInstaller/src/com/android/packageinstaller/InstallStaging.java
@@ -198,6 +198,11 @@
         params.setInstallerPackageName(intent.getStringExtra(
                 Intent.EXTRA_INSTALLER_PACKAGE_NAME));
         params.setInstallReason(PackageManager.INSTALL_REASON_USER);
+        // AxionOS: allow installing a lower versionCode over an existing app instead of
+        // failing INSTALL_FAILED_VERSION_DOWNGRADE. isDowngradePermitted() still requires
+        // either a debuggable build/app or INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE (system-initiated
+        // sessions only) before this actually takes effect.
+        params.setRequestDowngrade(true);
         // Disable full screen intent usage by for sideloads.
         params.setPermissionState(Manifest.permission.USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT,
                 PackageInstaller.SessionParams.PERMISSION_STATE_DENIED);
--- a/packages/PackageInstaller/src/com/android/packageinstaller/v2/model/InstallRepository.kt
+++ b/packages/PackageInstaller/src/com/android/packageinstaller/v2/model/InstallRepository.kt
@@ -470,6 +470,11 @@
         }
         params.setInstallerPackageName(intent.getStringExtra(Intent.EXTRA_INSTALLER_PACKAGE_NAME))
         params.setInstallReason(PackageManager.INSTALL_REASON_USER)
+        // AxionOS: allow installing a lower versionCode over an existing app instead of
+        // failing INSTALL_FAILED_VERSION_DOWNGRADE. isDowngradePermitted() still requires
+        // either a debuggable build/app or INSTALL_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE (system-initiated
+        // sessions only) before this actually takes effect.
+        params.setRequestDowngrade(true)
         // Disable full screen intent usage by for sideloads.
         params.setPermissionState(
             Manifest.permission.USE_FULL_SCREEN_INTENT, SessionParams.PERMISSION_STATE_DENIED
--
2.40.0
